    {
      "id": "u_2d2a5356e148827fc1657e16_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "For both __TRILIUM_PH_0__Render Note__TRILIUM_PH_1__ and more complicated scripts, it's generally useful to split the code into multiple __TRILIUM_PH_2__Code__TRILIUM_PH_3__ notes.",
      "sourceHash": "2d2a5356e148827fc1657e16fd35f567b1ca3963444d33d08aea1d7879df7d69",
      "context": "Script bundles",
      "contextHash": "b5dbc4d8c244a3badb06f1199001917726fd3726a763d8c102aab9336c5335bb",
      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
    },
    {
      "id": "u_351d66652cf9118d72c02e79_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "When a script is run, the sub-children of the script being run (or the __TRILIUM_PH_0__Render Note__TRILIUM_PH_1__) are checked for children. If the children are Code notes of the corresponding type (front-end or backend) as the code being run, they will be evaluated as well.",
      "sourceHash": "351d66652cf9118d72c02e796f08663c24d008dc40f60ae525fed1173e9bad2f",
      "context": "Script bundles",
      "contextHash": "b5dbc4d8c244a3badb06f1199001917726fd3726a763d8c102aab9336c5335bb",
      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
    },
    {
      "id": "u_d6eb7f2e91e637b65272c1ad_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "The collection of a script and its child notes is called a __TRILIUM_PH_0__bundle__TRILIUM_PH_1__. A child note inside a bundle is called a __TRILIUM_PH_2__module__TRILIUM_PH_3__.",
      "sourceHash": "d6eb7f2e91e637b65272c1add7e6ef677599d81145090e70207b7e34d9bd2764",
      "context": "Script bundles",
      "contextHash": "b5dbc4d8c244a3badb06f1199001917726fd3726a763d8c102aab9336c5335bb",
      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
    },
    {
      "id": "u_5dff21dbccc3e1509b99a4c0_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "As a basic example of dependencies, consider the following note structure:",
      "sourceHash": "5dff21dbccc3e1509b99a4c0631ea75936757a71206ca9fbcc16386c168eb2cc",
      "context": "Script bundles",
